/// A sample that covers every supported element.
const sampleMarkdown = r'''
# flutter_markdown_x

Converts Markdown into **Widgets**, *without going through an HTML string*.
~~Strikethrough~~, `inline code`, and [links](https://pub.dev) work too.
CJK text renders as well: 日本語のテキストも表示できます。
Emoji shortcodes too: :tada: :rocket: :+1: (but not in `:code:`).

## Images

A `data:` image (tap to be notified): ![Gradient](data:image/png;base64,)

With dimensions (`width` and `height`; if wider than the available space, it shrinks while keeping the aspect ratio):
<img src="data:image/png;base64," width="99999" height="49999" alt="Oversized dimensions">

Relative paths are resolved with `imageDirectory`. If an image cannot be loaded, the alt text is shown: ![Image that cannot be loaded](img/missing.png)

## inline HTML

H<sub>2</sub>O, E = mc<sup>2</sup>, <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>C</kbd>,
<mark>highlight</mark>, <u>underline</u>, <small>small text</small>.<br>
Use `<br>` for a line break. A <span style="color:#d1242f">color from the style attribute</span> and a
<span style="background-color:#fff8c5; color:#000; font-weight:bold">background color</span> are applied too.

<cite>cite</cite>, <dfn>dfn</dfn>, <var>var</var>, <samp>samp</samp>, <tt>tt</tt>, <big>big</big>,
<abbr title="HyperText Markup Language">HTML</abbr>, <q>a <q>nested</q> quote</q>,
<bdo dir="rtl">abc</bdo>, long<wbr>word.

<hr>

Footnotes[^1] and [reference links][pub] work as well.

<p align="center">A paragraph with align="center"</p>

<details>
<summary>Click to open <b>details</b></summary>

You can write **Markdown** inside.

- Item 1
- Item 2

</details>

## list

- Bulleted item
  - Nested
    1. Numbered
    2. Numbered
- [x] A completed task
- [ ] An incomplete task

## Blockquote

> A blockquote can contain **emphasis** and `code`.
>
> - Lists work too

## code block

```dart
void main() {
  final list = <int>[1, 2, 3].where((e) => e < 3 && e > 0);
  print(list);
}
```

## table

| Item | Align | Value |
|:-----|:-----:|------:|
| Left | Center | Right |
| `code` | **bold** | 1,234 |

HTML tables are supported too.

<table>
<tr><th>Tag</th><th align="center">Supported</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>&lt;table&gt;</code></td><td>○</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>&lt;details&gt;</code></td><td>○</td></tr>
</table>

## Code blocks (other languages)

```python
def greet(name: str) -> str:
    # comment
    return f"Hello, {name}" * 2
```

```json
{"name": "flutter_markdown_x", "version": 1, "fast": true}
```

## Math and diagrams

Inline math such as $e^{i\pi}+1=0$ and a block:

$$\int_0^1 x^2\,dx = \frac{1}{3}$$

```mermaid
graph TD
  A[Start] --> B{OK?}
  B -- yes --> C[Done]
  B -- no --> A
```

## Media

`<video>`, `<audio>`, `<iframe>`, `<embed>` and `<object>` become media blocks.
The package shows a link to the file; this app plugs in video_player for videos and pdfrx for PDFs,
and adds an icon to the other kinds.

<video src="https://flutter.github.io/assets-for-api-docs/assets/videos/butterfly.mp4" title="Butterfly (tap to play)" controls>
Your browser does not support video.
</video>

<audio controls>
<source src="https://example.com/media/podcast.mp3" type="audio/mpeg">
</audio>

<embed src="asset:assets/sample.pdf" type="application/pdf" title="Sample PDF">

<iframe src="https://example.com/embed/map" title="Embedded map"></iframe>

A media element inside a paragraph, such as <audio src="https://example.com/media/chime.mp3"></audio>, is an inline link.

## Alerts and citations

> [!TIP]
> GitHub-style alerts are shown with an icon and color for each kind.

Citations become small chips and notify on tap [1][2, 3].

---

Symbols such as 1 < 2 && 3 > 2 are shown as they are.

[pub]: https://pub.dev/packages/markdown

[^1]: Footnote definitions are shown together at the end of the document.
''';
